  "verbalization": "Thioguanine is implicated in the targeting of SK-HEP1 cells, which are known to be a model for cancer cell lines, and this relationship is supported by multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that thioguanine acts as a target for several compounds, including (2S,3R,5R)-2-[(R)-bromo-[(2R,3R,5S,6R)-3,5-dibromo-6-ethyloxan-2-yl]methyl]-5-[(1R)-1-bromoprop-2-ynyl]oxolan-3-ol, Massarinin B, and Digitoxigenin, all of which are known to target Tankyrase-2. This indicates that thioguanine may interact with Tankyrase-2 through a common mechanism, possibly by inhibiting its activity or by modulating its expression. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking thioguanine to Tankyrase-2 suggests a potential role in the regulation of gene expression, particularly in the context of cancer. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that thioguanine may exert its therapeutic effects through a mechanism involving Tankyrase-2, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
